Reports whether a \fBSplitBoundary\fP with the corresponding name exists inside the model\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class SPLITBOUNDARY_COMPLEX> pair< string, bool > \fBcsmp::SplitBoundaryInterface\fP< dim, SPLITBOUNDARY_COMPLEX >::CreateSplitBoundaryBetween (const char * region1_name, const char * region2_name)"

.PP
creates \fBSplitBoundary\fP between non-overlapping regions that share nodes at their perimeter; all shared nodes are multiplicated including perimeter nodes Creates \fBSplitBoundary\fP between two unique regions that share nodes along their perimeter\&. The first region will be placed on the inside of the new split boundary\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIregion1_name\fP name of the unique region that shall be on the inside of the new split boundary 
.br
\fIregion2_name\fP of the unique region that touches (shares nodes with) region1 and shall become the outside region of the new split boundary
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Method will add new \fBNode\fP and \fBInterFace\fP objects to the model

.PP
method does not create a temporary \fBBoundary\fP on the way to the \fBSplitBoundary\fP construction

.PP
method ignores Elements that are lines
.RE
.PP
